  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP Atlantic Corridor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norway&#x2019;s contribution is softly earmarked to Output 2 of the UNDP Atlantic Corridor Project implemented in Ghana, Togo and Benin and C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, focused on strengthening community resilience and engagement to prevent and respond to violent extremism in Benin, C&#xf4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Ghana and Togo to respond and prevent radicalization factors at the hyper-local levels. This project contributes to the three key sub-outputs of the Atlantic Corridor Project: Output 2.1 Strengthening early warning and response mechanisms and approaches to violent extremism, Output 2.2 Strengthening the socio-economic resilience of at-risk youth and women and other vulnerable populations in target locations; Output 2.3 Promoting alternative and counter-narrative messages to hate speech promoting violence and violent extremism.</narrative>
  </description>
